==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|osp|es}} {{m|osp|cridar|cridar, gridar|}}, from {{etyl|ML.|es}} {{m|la|crīdāre||to cry out, publish, proclaim}}, from {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|quirito||to shriek, hiss}}. 

An alternative (less likely) origin is {{etyl|frk|es}} *{{m|frk||krītan|}} "to cry out, scream, proclaim" (--Littré), related to {{cog|dum|critan|crītan|to cry}}.

Cognate wtih Portuguese {{m|pt|gritar}}, Catalan {{m|ca|cridar}}, French {{m|fr|crier}}, Italian {{m|it|gridare}}).

===Verb===
{{es-verb|grit|ar}}

# to [[shout]], to [[scream]], to [[cry]] out, to [[call out]]
# to [[jeer]] at

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj-ar|grit|combined=1}}

